WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.040
Abby Sciuto is TV's perkiest goth, a brilliant&nbsp;
scientist, and a shameless caffeine addict. We're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.600
here to give you the full story behind&nbsp;
NCIS' unforgettable forensic scientist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.920
from her trademark pigtails to the reason&nbsp;
her actress departed the show for good.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.440
While Abby might be well known for her cheery&nbsp;
disposition, she's also a serious-minded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.040
forensics-loving crime solver. This balance feels&nbsp;
very natural, and it's no mystery as to why:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.000
Her actress, Pauley Perrette, came to the&nbsp;
show with a degree in criminal justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.920
She had planned to go into law enforcement&nbsp;
before she got bit by the acting bug.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.200
Early roles on shows like&nbsp;
The Drew Carey Show, Jesse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.840
and Dawson's Creek finally culminated in&nbsp;
2003, when she landed the role of Abby.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.720
Abby's first appearance comes in a&nbsp;
two-part story in JAG's eighth season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.280
After a body is found near the Potomac River,&nbsp;
the JAG team calls in the investigative unit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.120
at NCIS to help them uncover the&nbsp;
truth of this suspicious death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.280
Our introduction to Abby is remarkable&nbsp;
to revisit: The character debuts nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.360
fully-formed. While we learn more about&nbsp;
her as the show's many seasons wind on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:11.680
Abby's most distinctive tics and trademarks&nbsp;
are all on display in her very first outing.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.760
"But for a dinner… Get me an ID in&nbsp;
two and I'll make it cafe atlantico."

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.960
The first scene featuring Abby shows&nbsp;
her calmly watching some guys blast a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.200
mannequin with a shotgun. Later, when she's&nbsp;
detailing some pretty gruesome x-rays,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.080
she shares the particulars of the damage in&nbsp;
a detached, almost bored-sounding deadpan.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.920
"That's a cross section of what&nbsp;
a 12 gauge did to an L3 to L5."

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.080
Right from the beginning, she's unlike&nbsp;
any other character on television.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.400
Though Abby's aesthetic affectations might lead a&nbsp;
viewer to assume she's gloomy and brooding, Abby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:54.560
is actually incredibly upbeat and happy. Though&nbsp;
she drives an Addams Family-esque Ford Model A,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.000
the death investigator is&nbsp;
an unusually bubbly type.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.800
"He wears $3000 Italian sunglasses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.000
and has Justin Beiber in his hard&nbsp;
drive. Can't we arrest him for that?"

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.280
Perrette has said that this perkiness was very&nbsp;
much a choice, and actually modeled after a dog.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.960
"I patterned everything [Abby] does&nbsp;
physically after this rescue dog that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.040
I had named CiCi. [...] So, the&nbsp;
way Abby stands — she stands very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.640
upright — and even the way she cocks her head.&nbsp;
Everything is done exactly like this dog."

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.960
Abby's energy is all natural, too:

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.760
"For the first six years it was&nbsp;
Hawaiian Punch, [...] but then I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.960
quit eating and drinking refined&nbsp;
sugar, so now I have unsweetened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.840
cranberry juice. [It tasted like]&nbsp;
five billion percent raw cranberries."

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.800
She loves extreme music, all-black outfits,&nbsp;
and spooky dolls. But there is one thing she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.080
regrets about her deathly lifestyle: A&nbsp;
prominent spider web tattoo on her neck.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.000
Perette doesn't have to reach too deep to&nbsp;
find that feeling in herself. The actress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.880
has been open about how much she hates having&nbsp;
the tattoo applied before filming every day.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.520
"Every day that I come to work,&nbsp;
I have to prepare myself for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.440
dreaded putting on of the neck&nbsp;
tattoo. I absolutely hate it."

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.040
Perrette added that she tried to get&nbsp;
the writers to add a tattoo removal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.440
arc to Abby's story, but they wouldn't budge.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.920
This is far from the only physical irritation&nbsp;
that Perette went through to play the character:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.000
Dyeing her hair black once led to&nbsp;
a disastrous allergic reaction:

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.240
"I dyed my hair on Wednesday, and I went to work&nbsp;
at five in the morning on a Thursday. [...] I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.760
would wake up the next morning and my&nbsp;
head was getting bigger and bigger".

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.040
It would be a real shame if&nbsp;
Perrette was putting all her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.920
actorly effort into a half-formed character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:34.880
Luckily, the writers of NCIS have been able to&nbsp;
give Abby quite a full life over 15 seasons.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.560
Abby is the adopted child of deaf parents,&nbsp;
therefore making her proficient in sign language.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.680
Abby's biological parents are deceased, though the&nbsp;
manner in which they passed is never discussed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.960
Born in New Orleans, the frequent&nbsp;
moves her parents made have given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.000
her a wide breadth of knowledge&nbsp;
about the southern United States.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.560
Her interest in forensics came from one&nbsp;
of the places she lived as a young girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.720
At one point, her family lived next door&nbsp;
to a wrecking yard. She found herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.360
wondering how the cars arriving at the yard&nbsp;
in such a twisted state became so mangled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.600
and eventually learned about&nbsp;
the field of forensics.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.360
Abby threw herself into her studies, graduating&nbsp;
from LSU with full honors and a bachelor's degree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:18.320
in sociology, criminology, and psychology. She&nbsp;
then earned her master's from Georgia State in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.440
criminology and forensic science. It is also&nbsp;
implied that she got a PhD in chemistry at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.760
several points throughout the series. Abby&nbsp;
was quickly snatched up by the NCIS team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.840
after graduating, becoming an integral&nbsp;
part of nearly all their investigations.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.480
Abby tends to work alone. She has good&nbsp;
reason to be wary of partners, though.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:42.320
At one point in the series, the NCIS team takes&nbsp;
on another forensics expert named Chip Sterling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.440
He works as Abby's assistant, though&nbsp;
she grumbles about the intrusion.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.040
The team's senior field agent, Tony DiNozzo ,&nbsp;
jokes about Sterling's relatively minor screw-ups.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.640
In time, Chip launches a plot&nbsp;
to frame Tony for murder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.600
apparently holding a grudge against him&nbsp;
from a time before he was on the NCIS team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.840
After this plot is revealed, Chip tries to&nbsp;
kill Abby to avoid being captured. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.160
avoiding her own death, Abby asks her director&nbsp;
if she can work alone from that point forward.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.400
Chip Sterling's attack wasn't the last&nbsp;
time someone would make an attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.200
on Abby Sciuto's life. A hitman comes&nbsp;
after Abby in the 15th season of NCIS.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:22.720
Her life is only saved by the intervention of an&nbsp;
MI6 agent named Clayton Reeves. After tricking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.160
the man who wanted her dead into revealing his&nbsp;
identity, Abby opts to retire from the NCIS.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.560
Though Abby spent 15 seasons with the&nbsp;
team, she says her goodbye off screen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:36.720
She leaves her bosses a note to let them&nbsp;
know she's gone, and heads to the UK.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:39.200
That's where the series&nbsp;
claims Abby is to this day.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.320
In the real world, Perrette's departure from the&nbsp;
show was a little more complicated than Abby's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.400
Abby's goodbye was written as a way&nbsp;
around having to put actor Mark Harmon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.720
and Perrette on set at the same time.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:55.280
Perrette claims that Harmon was physically&nbsp;
abusive to his costars and that he is the reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:59.600
she will never reprise her role on the&nbsp;
series. In a revealing social media post,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.240
Perrette made it clear that&nbsp;
she's afraid of Harmon.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.520
"NO I AM NOT COMING BACK! EVER! I have nightmares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:08.480
about it. [...] I have a new&nbsp;
show that is SAFE AND HAPPY!"

